title: Prime Minister's Questions
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/cards/commons_chamber.jpg
tags: commons
view-if: pmqs_timer <= 0
on-arrival: pmqs_timer = 2; month_actions += 1

= Prime Minister's Questions

Tuesday and Thursday, 3.15pm. [? if con_in_government = 0 : Callaghan is an old hand at the dispatch box, and he enjoys patronising you. ?][? if con_in_government = 1 : Now you are at the dispatch box, and [+ lab_leader +] is asking the questions. ?]

- @attack: Go on the attack.
- @careful: Stick to the detail.
- @easy_discard

@attack
on-arrival: {!
var chance = 45 + (Q.thatcher_rating - Q.lab_leader_rating);
if (!Q.con_in_government) {
    chance += 3 * Q.strike_wave;
} else if (Q.unemployment > 8) {
    chance -= 2 * (Q.unemployment - 8);
}
if (chance < 10) {
    chance = 10;
} else if (chance > 90) {
    chance = 90;
}
Q.pmq_success = (Math.random() * 100 < chance) ? 1 : 0;
!}
go-to: attack_win if pmq_success = 1; attack_lose if pmq_success = 0

@attack_win
on-arrival: thatcher_rating += 3; lab_leader_rating -= 2; rebellion -= 1 if con_in_government and rebellion > 0

[? if con_in_government = 0 : You land the blow. Callaghan's avuncular manner slips, and the sketch-writers notice. ?][? if con_in_government = 1 : You demolish [+ lab_leader +]'s question and turn it back on Labour. Our backbenchers wave their order papers. ?]

@attack_lose
on-arrival: thatcher_rating -= 2; lab_leader_rating += 1

[? if con_in_government = 0 : Callaghan swats the question aside with a joke at your expense. Labour's benches roar. ?][? if con_in_government = 1 : [+ lab_leader +] reads out the latest unemployment figures, and our own backbenchers stare at their shoes. ?]

@careful
on-arrival: thatcher_rating += 1

[? if con_in_government = 0 : A precise question on the money supply figures. The Prime Minister bluffs, and the people who matter notice. ?][? if con_in_government = 1 : Statistics, dates and figures. It isn't exciting, but no one lands a blow. ?]
